meta {
  name: 00 How to block and restore
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/subscription
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  READ THIS FIRST. It is the instructions for the rest of the folder, and it
  doubles as a working request so you can see the state you are about to change.

  Nothing in this folder waits 30 days. Status is computed from timestamps on
  every read — there is no stored status and no job — so moving a date IS the
  state change, and the very next request answers differently.

  ## Setup, once

  1. `Center Auth / 03 Login`      -> captures {{accessToken}} for the center
  2. `Center Students / 02 Provision student` -> captures {{activationKey}}
  3. `Student Activation / 01 Activate`       -> the student sets a password,
     AND this is what starts the trial clock for the center
  4. `Subscription Access / 01 Student login` -> captures the student tokens

  After step 3 this request returns TRIAL with `studentsMayLearn: true`.

  ## To block them

  Run this against the test database — the one in `.env.test`, which is what
  `npm run start:testdb` serves. Never the production one.

  ```sql
  -- Blocked: a paid period that lapsed more than 7 days ago, so it is past
  -- grace. Use -2 days instead of -8 to see GRACE_PERIOD, where they still
  -- learn.
  UPDATE center_subscriptions
     SET plan = 'PAID',
         paid_until = now() - interval '8 days',
         trial_started_at = NULL,
         trial_ends_at = NULL
   WHERE center_id = '<your center id>';
  ```

  `trial_*` are cleared because payment is checked first: a center that
  converted mid-trial is judged on what it paid for, so leaving a live trial in
  place would keep them on TRIAL and nothing would appear to happen.

  Get the center id from this request's own response, or:

  ```sql
  SELECT c.id, c.name FROM centers c ORDER BY c.created_at DESC LIMIT 5;
  ```

  ## To restore them

  ```sql
  UPDATE center_subscriptions
     SET paid_until = now() + interval '30 days'
   WHERE center_id = '<your center id>';
  ```

  Re-run `02 Learn` immediately. No restart, no re-login, no cache to clear.
  The student's existing access token keeps working, because the check happens
  on every request rather than at login — which is the whole point of Phase 5.

  ## Expected results

  | Request | Entitled | Blocked |
  |---|---|---|
  | 02 Learn                    | 200 | 403 SUBSCRIPTION_INACTIVE |
  | 03 Refresh                  | 201 | 201, reporting BLOCKED |
  | 04 Create speaking room     | 201 | 403 SUBSCRIPTION_INACTIVE |
  | 05 Center provisions        | 201 | 403 SUBSCRIPTION_INACTIVE |
  | 06 Center reads subscription| 200 | 200 |

  The last two rows are the interesting pair. A blocked center cannot hand out
  new access, but keeps its whole dashboard — because the thing it most needs
  to do is pay, and locking it out of the page that leads there makes that less
  likely, not more.
}
